This repository is under two licenses, and a few files keep an upstream license.

- CC-BY-4.0: the prose, prompts, notes, reports, configs and run data.
  Text: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt
- MIT: the code (bin/, the Python under report/ and tests/, install.py, CI and hooks).
  Text: LICENSES/MIT.txt
- Upstream material keeps its license. Lines from slop-code-bench's prompts and the
  patches to its source are MIT (Copyright (c) 2025 gabeorlanski). Patches to the
  problem set and the problem text in outputs/ are Apache-2.0 (gabeorlanski/scb-problems).
  Text: LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt

REUSE.toml says which license covers each path; `uvx reuse lint` checks it.

Copyright 2026 Jason Carver.
